    "narrative": "The lineup for LawDog today is headlined by **Bryson Stott** (72.63) and **Taylor Ward** (69.73), both of whom benefit from favorable matchups against mediocre arms. **Bryson Stott** is an elite play today, as the 18% boost from facing a pitcher with a 4.73 xERA outweighs his lower spot in the order. Similarly, **Taylor Ward** is poised for a big day; he is playing in a stadium that provides a 16% park factor bump, and his 15% efficiency gain against a pitcher with a 4.60 xERA makes him an essential start. **Brendan Donovan** also rounds out the top tier with a 67.45 score, bolstered by a 14% platoon advantage and a 10% boost for hitting at the top of the lineup.\n\nOur most difficult bench decision involved choosing between our active utility spot and **Gavin Sheets**, who narrowly missed the cut with a score of 51.44. While **Gavin Sheets** provides solid platoon utility, the daily efficiency model favors the slightly higher floor of **Geraldo Perdomo** and **Luis Arraez** to anchor our average and speed categories. We are proceeding with **Wenceel Perez** despite the lineup currently being pending; if he does not draw into the starting nine, he will be swapped to minimize dead roster spots. Conversely, **Masyn Winn** is a high-value play today; while facing a pitcher with a 4.84 xERA, his aggressive base-stealing profile is amplified by a 90% slow-delivery pitcher efficiency, giving us a rare edge in our scarcest category. Be advised that **Jung Hoo Lee** and **Daulton Varsho** are facing a catcher with a sub-1.90s pop time, which slightly caps their stolen base upside, but their overall platoon edges remain strong enough to keep them firmly in the starting rotation.",
